# Rule Validation and Quality Assurance

## Purpose
Automated validation rules and quality checks to ensure all cursor rules comply with rule management guidelines.

## Scope
This rule covers validation patterns, quality checks, and automated compliance verification for cursor rules.

## Required Rule Structure Validation

### Metadata Header Validation
Every rule MUST have a complete metadata header:

```yaml
---
title: "Rule Title"                    # Required: Clear, descriptive title
description: "Brief description"       # Required: What the rule covers
version: "1.0.0"                      # Required: Semantic versioning
category: "core|templates|plugins|addons|utilities|management"  # Required: Valid category
tags: ["tag1", "tag2"]                # Optional: Relevant tags
dependencies: ["../other-rule.mdc"]    # Optional: Rule dependencies
alwaysApply: true|false               # Optional: Loading behavior
---
```

### Required Sections Validation
Every rule MUST contain these sections:

1. **Purpose** - Clear statement of what the rule covers
2. **Scope** - What is included/excluded from the rule
3. **Related Rules** - Cross-references to other relevant rules
4. **Rule Dependencies** - Which rules this rule depends on

## Cross-Reference Validation Rules

### No Circular References
```markdown
# ❌ INVALID - Circular reference
Rule A references Rule B
Rule B references Rule A

# ✅ VALID - One-way reference
Rule A references Rule B
Rule B does not reference Rule A
```

### Valid Path References
```markdown
# ✅ VALID - Correct relative paths
- [Core Rule](../core/rule-name.mdc)
- [Plugin Rule](../plugins/plugin-name.mdc)
- [Utility Rule](../utilities/utility-name.mdc)

# ❌ INVALID - Broken paths
- [Rule](rule-name.mdc)  # Missing directory
- [Rule](core/rule-name.mdc)  # Missing ../
```

### Dependency Accuracy
```yaml
# Metadata dependencies MUST match actual rule dependencies
dependencies: ["../core/error-handling.mdc"]

# Rule Dependencies section MUST reference the same rules
## Rule Dependencies
This rule extends:
- [Error Handling](../core/error-handling.mdc) - Uses error handling patterns
```

## Content Quality Validation

### Code Example Validation
```lua
-- ✅ VALID - Complete, functional example
function ExampleFunction()
    if condition then
        return true
    end
    return false
end

-- ❌ INVALID - Incomplete example
function ExampleFunction()
    if condition then
        -- Missing implementation
    end
end
```

### Best Practices Validation
Every rule MUST include:
- **Clear examples** with complete code
- **Error handling** patterns where applicable
- **Configuration integration** examples
- **Best practices** section with do's and don'ts

## Automated Validation Checklist

### Pre-Commit Validation
Before committing any rule changes:

- [ ] **Metadata Complete**: All required metadata fields present
- [ ] **Valid Category**: Category is one of the approved values
- [ ] **Semantic Version**: Version follows MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH format
- [ ] **Required Sections**: Purpose, Scope, Related Rules, Rule Dependencies present
- [ ] **No Circular References**: Check all cross-references for circularity
- [ ] **Valid Paths**: All cross-references use correct relative paths
- [ ] **Dependency Accuracy**: Metadata dependencies match rule dependencies
- [ ] **Complete Examples**: All code examples are functional and complete
- [ ] **Error Handling**: Error handling patterns included where needed
- [ ] **Best Practices**: Clear guidance on do's and don'ts

### Monthly Audit Validation
During monthly rule audits:

- [ ] **Cross-Reference Integrity**: All referenced rules exist and are accessible
- [ ] **Content Freshness**: Examples and patterns are current
- [ ] **No Duplication**: Content is not duplicated across multiple rules
- [ ] **Consistent Naming**: All rule names follow kebab-case convention
- [ ] **Proper Categorization**: Rules are in correct category directories
- [ ] **alwaysApply Optimization**: Loading behavior is appropriate for rule type

## Validation Error Prevention

### Common Violations to Avoid

#### 1. Missing Required Sections
```markdown
# ❌ INVALID - Missing sections
# Rule content without Purpose, Scope, Related Rules, Rule Dependencies

# ✅ VALID - Complete structure
## Purpose
Clear statement of rule purpose

## Scope
What the rule covers

## Related Rules
- [Other Rule](../path/rule.mdc) - Description

## Rule Dependencies
This rule extends:
- [Dependency Rule](../path/dependency.mdc) - Description
```

#### 2. Broken Cross-References
```markdown
# ❌ INVALID - Broken references
- [Non-existent Rule](../core/non-existent.mdc)
- [Wrong Path](wrong/path/rule.mdc)

# ✅ VALID - Working references
- [Existing Rule](../core/existing-rule.mdc)
- [Correct Path](../plugins/plugin-rule.mdc)
```

#### 3. Incomplete Examples
```lua
-- ❌ INVALID - Incomplete example
function IncompleteExample()
    -- Missing implementation
end

-- ✅ VALID - Complete example
function CompleteExample()
    if not HasPlugin("PluginName") then
        yield("/echo [Script] Plugin not available")
        return false
    end
    
    return true
end
```

## Quality Metrics and Monitoring

### Validation Success Rate
Track the percentage of rules passing validation:
- **Target**: 100% of rules pass all validation checks
- **Measurement**: Monthly audit results
- **Action**: Fix violations immediately when discovered

### Cross-Reference Accuracy
Monitor the health of cross-references:
- **Target**: 100% of cross-references are valid
- **Measurement**: Automated link checking
- **Action**: Update broken references immediately

### Content Quality Score
Assess the quality of rule content:
- **Target**: All rules have complete, functional examples
- **Measurement**: Manual review of examples and patterns
- **Action**: Improve content quality through iterative updates

